# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# local.properties.example — bootstrap-android-scaffold, PR 1 (scaffold-build).
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE. Copy it to `local.properties` at the repo root and
# replace the placeholder with the absolute path to your Android SDK install.
#
#   cp local.properties.example local.properties
#   $EDITOR local.properties
#
# `local.properties` itself is in `.gitignore` (machine-specific paths never
# belong in version control). Android Studio writes this file automatically on
# first sync, but committing the example lets:
#
#   * CI pick up the SDK path from `ANDROID_HOME` / `ANDROID_SDK_ROOT` instead
#     of relying on a checked-in `local.properties`.
#   * New contributors bootstrap a working build without an IDE round-trip.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Path to the Android SDK install.
## Examples per platform (replace with your actual install path):
##   macOS:   /Users/<you>/Library/Android/sdk
##   Linux:   /home/<you>/Android/Sdk
##   Windows: C\:\\Users\\<you>\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\Sdk
sdk.dir=/path/to/Android/sdk